            119
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Information Related to Location of Endangered Species to Which Alternative DO criteria from the Regional Criteria Apply and Determining Whether DO Values Have Decreased Below the Baseline Distribution",
        "bbox": [
            111,
            133,
            877,
            188
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The map below shows the portion of the Suwannee, Santa Fe, New, and Withlacoochee North Rivers utilized by the Gulf Sturgeon and oval pigtoe mussel.",
        "bbox": [
            112,
            205,
            857,
            242
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/7e6f782f8773af1cf17f331a33c6d24f6773eb08280d0d9c86ff4e7a0a5c4040.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "image_footnote": [],
        "content": "",
        "bbox": [
            122,
            244,
            831,
            796
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "To evaluate whether DO values have decreased below the baseline distribution, it is recommended that a) no more than 10 percent of the DO daily average values be below the 10<sup>th</sup> percentile of the existing data distribution for that river segment, b) no more than 50 percent of the daily average values to be below the median of the existing data distribution for that river",
        "bbox": [
            111,
            811,
            870,
            886
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "segment. The $1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ percentiles and median DO values for each of the affected river segments are provided in Table 3.",
        "bbox": [
            111,
            90,
            874,
            127
        ],
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "When assessing these waters in the future, compliance with both the $1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ percentile and median DO values will be evaluated using a binomial hypothesis test at the 80 percent and 90 percent confidence levels necessary to place a water segment on the Planning List and Verified Lists, respectively, for TMDL development. The use of the binomial hypothesis test is consistent with the assessment for other water quality parameters conducted under Chapter 62-303, F.A.C. The number of exceedances required to have 80 percent and 90 percent confidence that more than 10 percent of the daily average values are below the applicable $1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }$ percentile value are provided in Chapter 62-303, F.A.C., Tables 1 and 3, respectively. The number exceedances required to have 80 percent and 90 percent confidence that more than 50 percent of the daily average values are below the applicable median value for sample sizes up to 419 are provided in Table 4.",
        "bbox": [
            111,
            142,
            880,
            320
        ],
        "page_idx": 2
    },
